admin queue; validating clears it, refusing takes the chef offline; an admin-deactivated chef is never auto-reactivated."}, {"id": "agents_chef_documents_append_only", "label": "Append-only chef_documents owned by the chef profile from first upload", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The candidature and the living dossier are the same rows so history cannot drift; missing is derived, never stored."}, {"id": "agents_messaging", "label": "In-house messaging (chef_client and support conversations)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stream was dropped; one conversation per (client, chef profile) pair; one writer (MessagingService.postMessage); a conversation the caller is not part of is 404; writable while a booking is pending or confirmed and 14 days after completion."}, {"id": "agents_contact_masking_when_served", "label": "Contact details masked when served, not when stored", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "messages.body is always what was written; a detected phone or email is served masked and the conversation flagged for admins, who read the original; regex detection is deterrence, not a guarantee."}, {"id": "agents_j2_contact_release", "label": "J-2 contact release (48h before a confirmed booking)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing is stored: moving or cancelling the booking changes the answer."}, {"id": "agents_redis_optional", "label": "Redis optional (in-process fallback for messaging rate limit and events)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With REDIS_URL the 20/minute send limit and events are shared between instances; without it both are in-process, fine for one instance and wrong for two."}, {"id": "agents_admin_chefs_back_office", "label": "Batch cookers in the back office (LF-0164, GET /admin/chefs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built on chef_profiles, not candidatures, so pre-FLOW-01 profiles are listed; STATE_WHERE is the single definition of online/offline/suspended/pending for filter, counts and rows; deleted accounts never listed."}, {"id": "agents_contact_forms", "label": "Contact forms: stored first, emailed second", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An email outage never loses a message; rate-limited per IP and per email with a honeypot; a reply is emailed before it is recorded so a failed send stores nothing (503 EMAIL_NOT_SENT)."}, {"id": "agents_audit_log", "label": "audit_log: compliance journal and debugging trail", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Railway log retention is short and cannot be queried by candidature; audit_log records reads, decisions, approvals, suspensions and failures, keyed by x-request-id."}, {"id": "agents_legacy_tables_renamed_aside", "label": "Legacy tables renamed aside to *_legacy, not dropped", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "AGENTS.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unused spec_domain tables co